# Wake the Sound BlasterX G6 and force a clean audio enumeration once per
# boot. The service is asynchronous: it is not ordered before the display
# manager, and no target pulls it in, so it cannot delay boot.
#
# The G6's HID endpoint is dead until a USBDEVFS_RESET, and its first audio
# enumeration reports an illegal UAC clock source until a re-enumeration.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="041e", ATTR{idProduct}=="3256", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="g6-coldboot-prep.service"

# 99-g6-coldboot.conf blacklists snd-usb-audio so it cannot probe the G6's
# first, cold-boot enumeration (which logs "selector reported illegal value"
# and creates a card with a broken clock tree). The G6's HID interfaces still
# bind through usbhid. g6-coldboot-prep.sh loads snd-usb-audio explicitly
# after the clean re-enumeration, so the driver only ever probes a valid
# clock tree.
#
# Consequence: the blacklist is per module, not per device. If the G6 is not
# attached at boot the prep never runs, so no other USB audio device gets the
# driver either. Run "sudo modprobe snd-usb-audio" once, or attach the G6
# once and let the prep run. This is stated in the installer prompt too.
